  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Performing Hysteria has already shown a clear footprint as an openly accessible scholarly book, with strong download activity, early citation uptake, and visible circulation in public knowledge spaces such as Wikipedia. Its record suggests a work that is being read, referenced, and used across adjacent fields rather than remaining confined to one discipline.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Published by Leuven University Press in 2020, Performing Hysteria brings a cross-disciplinary lens to contemporary images and representations of hysteria at a moment when the term is actively mobilized in public debate. The book\u2019s intellectual reach is reflected in its subject profile, which links hysteria with psychoanalysis, psychology, and philosophy, and in its open-access availability, which lowers barriers to use and reuse.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest evidence of impact is its sustained readership: the book has been downloaded 7,224 times through OAPEN. That level of use indicates substantial practical attention for a scholarly monograph and suggests that the book has found an audience beyond immediate citation. Its accessibility is reinforced by the record of open instances in repository infrastructure, supporting broad discoverability and reengagement.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Citation activity is still modest but real, with seven citations recorded in OpenAlex. Those citations arrive across articles, a book, and a dissertation, pointing to uptake in both scholarly and postgraduate research settings. The citing venues and concepts show especially close engagement with psychoanalysis, gender and sexuality, performance and media studies, and related discussions of clinical and cultural discourse.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The book also appears in public-facing knowledge infrastructure: Wikipedia mentions are present, indicating that its ideas have entered broader reference use. Combined with the citations, this suggests a work that is helping shape how hysteria is discussed across academic and public contexts, even though the evidence base remains relatively early.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, Performing Hysteria presents a pattern of emerging influence: widely accessed, cited in relevant interdisciplinary research, and visible in public knowledge environments. The record supports a narrative of growing scholarly and public relevance, with the clearest signals coming from open-access use and cross-field citation rather than from formal event or media coverage.</p>",
